/**
 * ServiceNow Background Script: Generate Demo Event Management Records
 *
 * Purpose: Creates 5 em_event records per CI in the target list,
 *          distributed across a realistic range of severities, with at
 *          least 1 Critical severity event guaranteed per CI.
 *
 *   Slot distribution (5 per CI):
 *   [1]  Critical   — severity: 6  GUARANTEED per CI
 *   [2]  Major      — severity: 5
 *   [3]  Minor      — severity: 4  (random within 3-4)
 *   [4]  Warning    — severity: 3  (random within 2-3)
 *   [5]  Clear      — severity: 1  (event resolved / self-healed)
 *
 * Instructions:
 *   1. Navigate to System Definition > Scripts - Background
 *   2. Paste this script and click "Run script"
 *   3. Adjust CONFIG values if needed before running
 *
 * Compatible with: ServiceNow Rome / San Diego / Tokyo / Utah / Vancouver+
 *
 * ServiceNow em_event severity values (OOTB):
 *   1 = Clear   2 = Indeterminate   3 = Warning
 *   4 = Minor   5 = Major           6 = Critical
 *
 * Event type values (em_event.type — free text / choice list):
 *   Common values: CPU, Memory, Disk, Network, Application,
 *                  Database, Security, Availability
 */

